Backport of chromeos-6.12 fef12e5a923e ("FROMLIST: tools/resolve_btfids:
Fix build when cross compiling kernel with clang", Suleiman Souhlal).

The cros kernel build passes CLANG_CROSS_FLAGS=--target=<cross> on the
make command line, which propagates through MAKEFLAGS into the
resolve_btfids sub-makes. tools/scripts/Makefile.include then adds it to
the HOST libbpf/libsubcmd CFLAGS, so the host tool gets cross-compiled
against the host sysroot and fails (__float128 unsupported, incomplete
user_pt_regs, -Wformat errors). Only built when CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_BTF=y
(needed for AOSP13/tm bpfloader).

Index: kernel-rockchip/tools/bpf/resolve_btfids/Makefile
===================================================================
--- kernel-rockchip.orig/tools/bpf/resolve_btfids/Makefile
+++ kernel-rockchip/tools/bpf/resolve_btfids/Makefile
@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@

 # Overrides for the prepare step libraries.
 HOST_OVERRIDES := AR="$(HOSTAR)" CC="$(HOSTCC)" LD="$(HOSTLD)" ARCH="$(HOSTARCH)" \
-		  CROSS_COMPILE="" EXTRA_CFLAGS="$(HOSTCFLAGS)"
+		  CROSS_COMPILE="" CLANG_CROSS_FLAGS="" EXTRA_CFLAGS="$(HOSTCFLAGS)"

 RM      ?= rm
 HOSTCC  ?= gcc
